## Symptom

Every `KubeAggregator` cross-reference resolves to a class that does not exist,
so inflating an `APIService` dies the same way ticket #1 does:

```
Can't locate IO/K8s/Api/KubeAggregator/V1/APIServiceSpec.pm in @INC
```

Four declarations are affected:

| file | line | declares | resolves to (wrong) |
|---|---|---|---|
| `KubeAggregator/.../V1/APIService.pm` | 15 | `KubeAggregator::V1::APIServiceSpec` | `IO::K8s::Api::KubeAggregator::V1::APIServiceSpec` |
| `KubeAggregator/.../V1/APIService.pm` | 23 | `KubeAggregator::V1::APIServiceStatus` | `IO::K8s::Api::KubeAggregator::V1::APIServiceStatus` |
| `KubeAggregator/.../V1/APIServiceSpec.pm` | 38 | `KubeAggregator::V1::ServiceReference` | `IO::K8s::Api::KubeAggregator::V1::ServiceReference` |
| `KubeAggregator/.../V1/APIServiceStatus.pm` | 6 | `['KubeAggregator::V1::APIServiceCondition']` | `IO::K8s::Api::KubeAggregator::V1::APIServiceCondition` |

The classes themselves are shipped and fine — they live under
`IO::K8s::KubeAggregator::Pkg::Apis::Apiregistration::V1::`. Only the resolution
is wrong.

## Cause

`_expand_class` in `lib/IO/K8s/Resource.pm:88` matches a prefix with:

```perl
if ($short =~ /^([A-Z][a-z]+)::/) {
```

`[A-Z][a-z]+` is one capital followed by lowercase only, so it cannot match a
CamelCase prefix. For `KubeAggregator::V1::APIServiceSpec` it tries to match
`Kube` and then requires `::`, finds `A`, and fails. Expansion falls through to
the default on line 97:

```perl
return "IO::K8s::Api::$short";
```

That makes the `'KubeAggregator' => 'IO::K8s::KubeAggregator::Pkg::Apis::Apiregistration'`
entry in `%_class_prefix` (line 41) dead code — it can never be reached. It is
the only CamelCase key in the map, which is why this is the only namespace hit.

## How it was found

Scanning all 744 shipped modules for attribute types whose target class is not
loadable (script: `scratchpad/find-missing-classes.pl`). Same sweep that
confirmed ticket #1's four missing classes; these five are the remainder.

## Suggested direction

Widen the prefix pattern to accept CamelCase (`^([A-Z]\w+?)::` with the map
lookup deciding, or match the longest key in `%_class_prefix` instead of
regex-guessing the prefix). Prefer a fix that cannot silently fall through:
today an unknown prefix produces a plausible-but-wrong class name and the error
only appears much later, at inflate time, as a missing file.

A guard test belongs with this: walk `%IO::K8s::Resource::_attr_registry` after
loading everything and assert every referenced class is loadable. That is a
cheap check that would have caught this, ticket #1 and the `StorageVersionSpec`
issue at build time.
